~ start
I want to go home. 

RITCHIE: Hey!

RITCHIE: Ollie!

OLLIE: ...

RITCHIE: There you are!

OLLIE: Ritchie...?

RITCHIE: Duh. Who else? Your imaginary friend? 

OLLIE: Where did everyone go?

RITCHIE: They all ran to the canteen to buy ice candy but the line was already so long! I didn't want to wait for that.
RITCHIE: …
RITCHIE: Hmm… You look weird.
RITCHIE: Don't tell me your tummy is doing a remix right now after finishing that entire bag of chicharon I gave you earlier? 

OLLIE: No.

RITCHIE: Wow. Your nose is going to reach the ceiling from lying, you know. 

OLLIE: I'm not lying!

RITCHIE: Weh? Are you sure? You know, when you were swallowing that one last piece earlier, your face looked like a deflated fishball.

- I'm not! 
	OLLIE: I'm not! Remember, the fable, The Turtle and the Monkey from Grade 1? Turtles are so cool and that’s why I'm trying act like one! See? I'm perfectly fine! 
	RITCHIE: Since when do turtles turn bright red and look like they're about to cry? 

- My face is totally normal! 
	OLLIE: My face is totally normal! If I say my tummy hurts, Nanay will get stressed and buy expensive medicine. I'll just be a big headache to them. 
	RITCHIE: Your eyes are already watery from the chili powder. Just admit it already!

OLLIE: Well, your face looks like a crushed piece of chicharon that got stepped on!

RITCHIE: Hey, that’s foul! I’m telling Mom!
RITCHIE: But at least I have a backup. 

OLLIE: You still have more?

RITCHIE: Bleeeh! I got 3 packs for only P20 from Aling Nena earlier using my extra baon! I only gave you one pack.

OLLIE: No fair! I thought we shared everything!

RITCHIE: I saved it.

OLLIE: For what?

RITCHIE: For me.

OLLIE: ?!

RITCHIE: Change topic! Your birthday is on November 8, right?

OLLIE: Yeah, I know. I'm old already.

RITCHIE: That’s in a few days! Are you having a birthday party? Will there be sweet spaghetti with hotdogs?

OLLIE: I don't know. Nanay hasn't told me yet. Maybe it's just simple or we’ll just have to order Jabi for this year again.

RITCHIE: You don't know?

- I don't want to ask them for too much. 
	OLLIE:  I don't want to ask them for too much. Money is hard and I don't want to be a headache for her and Tatay.
	RICTHIE: You think too much like a grown-up. We’re just kids. You're supposed to demand hotdogs on a stick! 
 
- I do want my own birthday party ... 
	OLLIE: I do want my own birthday party ... that I secretly drew a picture of a birthday party in my diary last night. It was fun imagining it but I closed the page quickly so Nanay wouldn't see it. 
	RITCHIE: See? I knew it! Okay, if you behave, I'll pray to the angels to make your wish come true!

RITCHIE: Well, if you do have a party, you have to invite me, okay? I'm your best friend after all. Heh.

OLLIE: Of course! Obviously you're invited.

RITCHIE: Hehe. I'm expecting chocolate cake! The one with marshmallows on top.

OLLIE: You just want cake!

RITCHIE: Obviously! That's free food, duh.
RITCHIE: But seriously, what do you really want for your birthday anyway?

OLLIE: I don't know. I really don't know.

RITCHIE: You always say "I don't know." Fine, I'll just pick something for you.

OLLIE: What is it?

RITCHIE: It's a secret! No clues so it's exciting.

OLLIE: Hey, that's unfair! Tell me!

RITCHIE: I don't want to. Too bad!
 
#BELL RINGS

RITCHIE: Oh no, we're dead! That's the bell! We're gonna be late, Ma'am is gonna get us!

OLLIE: Hey, wait! Don’t leave me!

=> END